ida: heads-up: the .NET quickstart and the CLI example in README.md got out of sync and our sample-app job failed on onboarding smoke tests this morning.

pranav: what exactly is out of date?

ida: a couple of small but fatal things: README shows `REDWOOD_API_KEY` for env and uses the old fluent API `new RedwoodClient(apiKey)`; the current SDK expects `REDWOOD_TOKEN` and `RedwoodClient.Create(new RedwoodOptions{Token = "..."})`. Also the CLI example still references `redwood-cli v0.3` which no longer accepts `--key` flag (it uses `--token` now).

ellen: ah yep, I saw failing logs: `ArgumentException: Missing token` and `Unknown option '--key'`. The snippet-runner reported the CLI exit code 2.

ida: broken snippet from README:```csharp
using Redwood;

var client = new RedwoodClient(Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REDWOOD_API_KEY"));
var res = client.Generate("hello");
Console.WriteLine(res.Text);
```

ida: and broken CLI example:```
# install
pipx install redwood-cli==0.3

# run
redwood-cli --key $REDWOOD_API_KEY generate "hello"
```

pranav: proposed fixes: switch env var name, update the constructor call, show async usage (we prefer async in docs), and update CLI flag. Also add a short migration note and a CI lint that checks quickstarts for env var names.

ellen: suggested .NET snippet:```csharp
using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Redwood;

class Program {
  static async Task Main() {
    var token = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REDWOOD_TOKEN"); // v1.0 rename
    var client = RedwoodClient.Create(new RedwoodOptions { Token = token });
    var resp = await client.GenerateAsync(new GenerateRequest { Prompt = "hello" });
    Console.WriteLine(resp.Text);
  }
}
```

ellen: and CLI fix:```
# install
pipx install redwood-cli==1.0

# run
redwood-cli --token $REDWOOD_TOKEN generate "hello"
```

pranav: I'll open a tiny PR to update quickstart-dotnet.md and the README examples, add a migration note in the upgrade guide, and include a unit check that runs the CLI example with `--help` and validates flags so we catch flag drift.

snippet-bot: @pranav opened PR #1203 updating quickstart-dotnet.md and README. Snippet-checker validation: CLI flag check failed locally but fixed in PR.

docs-bot: PR #1203 merged. CI added a README-snippet lint that verifies env var names match SDK expected names. Follow-up issue #1277 created to extend the CLI flag checker to all language quickstarts.

ida: thanks everyone  small docs drifts like this cause a lot of onboarding friction. Nice to have the snippet-check guard now.

pranav: yep, will follow up on #1277 next week. :shipit:
